% A setpagedevice whose maker fails leaves the incumbent device painting.
% Run against a live device (-d <dev>) by run-setpagedevice-failure-test.sh:
% prints SUCCESS iff every step holds.
%
% setpagedevice replaces the device in the graphics state, and the outgoing
% one is retired so its buffers are released. A maker can still fail at run
% time after the request has been accepted as well formed -- no display to
% open, an output path that will not take a file, dimensions that admit no
% buffer -- and PostScript lets the program catch that error and carry on.
% What it carries on with has to be the device it already had: retiring the
% incumbent before the replacement exists leaves the graphics state naming a
% device whose buffers are freed, and the next mark reads freed memory.
%
% The request below is well formed -- pgm is a device every build of this
% interpreter can select -- so it passes the roster check and reaches the
% maker, which then fails because no raster can be built at the page size
% asked for. A device is made before the incumbent is retired, so this is
% the moment the incumbent has to survive.

/getdevice { DEVICE } def

/before getdevice def

% An operator that fails part way leaves its own working operands behind;
% stopped reports the failure but does not rewind the stack, so the caught
% branch clears what is left. Named definitions are untouched by clear.
{ << /OutputDevice /pgm
     /PageSize [-100 -100] >> setpagedevice } stopped
    { clear }
    { (FAILURE: the maker was expected to fail and did not) = quit }
ifelse

% the incumbent is still the current device, the same object as before
before getdevice eq not
    { (FAILURE: the current device was replaced by a failed setpagedevice) = quit }
if

% and it still paints: on a retired device this is a read of freed memory
newpath 0 setgray 10 10 100 100 rectfill
20 20 moveto 80 80 lineto stroke
showpage

% a second page proves the device survived the page it just emitted
0.5 setgray 30 30 60 60 rectfill
showpage

count 0 eq
    { (SUCCESS) = }
    { (FAILURE: operand stack unbalanced) = }
ifelse
